WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:04.430
Shocking as it may seem, Cameron Diaz hasn't
starred in a major motion picture release

00:00:04.430 --> 00:00:08.069
since 2014, when she appeared in the reboot
of Annie.

00:00:08.069 --> 00:00:11.780
It's hard to believe that the woman who could
pretty much act in anything -- from rom-coms

00:00:11.780 --> 00:00:17.040
to sci-fi mindbenders to big-budget action
vehicles and raunchy comedies -- has virtually

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:18.040
disappeared.

00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:21.360
But there are lots of possible reasons why
one of Hollywood's "It" girls has backed away

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:22.660
from the screen scene.

00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:27.090
From typecasting to lifestyle changes, let's
take a look at all the reasons why Cameron

00:00:27.090 --> 00:00:31.390
Diaz has gone from being one of Hollywood's
busiest actresses to barely there.

00:00:31.390 --> 00:00:32.949
Critical downswing

00:00:32.949 --> 00:00:35.739
Diaz's critical reception has been hit or
miss over the years.

00:00:35.739 --> 00:00:39.629
At the turn of the millennium she was wowing
reviewers with her work in films like There's

00:00:39.629 --> 00:00:43.040
Something About Mary, Being John Malkovich,
and Vanilla Sky.

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:46.579
But her charms wore off somewhere around the
middle of the decade because her films started

00:00:46.579 --> 00:00:50.449
getting leveled by reviewers after her 2005
dramedy In Her Shoes.

00:00:50.449 --> 00:00:55.060
Diaz's most recent flicks have been especially
painful, garnering some of the worst marks

00:00:55.060 --> 00:00:56.460
of her entire career.

00:00:56.460 --> 00:00:59.149
These include Gambit, Annie, and 2013's The
Counselor.

00:00:59.149 --> 00:01:03.100
"You don't think that's a bit cold?"

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:06.070
"I think truth has no temperature."

00:01:06.070 --> 00:01:10.030
To her credit, though, Diaz can still turn
a mediocre movie into a box-office hit when

00:01:10.030 --> 00:01:11.030
it counts.

00:01:11.030 --> 00:01:16.390
Despite middling reviews, Bad Teacher surpassed
the coveted $100 million mark in 2011, and

00:01:16.390 --> 00:01:20.720
she found similar success with the 2014 release
of The Other Woman.

00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:23.850
The problem is, for every hit she's had, she's
had just as many flops.

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:27.811
The same year The Other Woman came out, Diaz
starred in the underwhelming Sex Tape, which

00:01:27.811 --> 00:01:32.220
was ripped to shreds by critics and earned
disappointing returns at the box office.

00:01:32.220 --> 00:01:35.930
Even the movie-musical Annie failed to catch
on with audiences or reviewers.

00:01:35.930 --> 00:01:40.590
In other words: Diaz may no longer be bankable
on just her star power alone.

00:01:40.590 --> 00:01:41.730
Evolving interests

00:01:41.730 --> 00:01:47.890
When Cameron Diaz made her feature film debut
in 1994's The Mask, she was just 22 years

00:01:47.890 --> 00:01:48.890
old.

00:01:48.890 --> 00:01:51.060
And even then her role choices were often
interesting.

00:01:51.060 --> 00:01:55.500
She starred in a few dark comedies like The
Last Supper and Head Above Water before becoming

00:01:55.500 --> 00:01:58.250
a mainstream sensation in My Best Friend's
Wedding.

00:01:58.250 --> 00:02:01.820
Even as she fell into the cheesy romantic
comedy trap of the '90s, she made sure to

00:02:01.820 --> 00:02:04.290
mix in roles with some real meat in them when
she could.

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:08.729
Nowadays, she seems to have even less patience
for paper thin parts than before, even though

00:02:08.729 --> 00:02:11.569
those are the ones that help to keep the lights
on most often.

00:02:11.569 --> 00:02:14.299
As she told Collider of her decision to star
in The Other Woman:

00:02:14.299 --> 00:02:18.689
"Usually, when it's a story about three women
all being involved with the same man, it ends

00:02:18.689 --> 00:02:22.069
in some eyeballs being scratched out and some
weaves being snatched off.

00:02:22.069 --> 00:02:24.510
We decided that wasn't the story we wanted
to tell."

00:02:24.510 --> 00:02:28.130
She said the film was more about how the women
"empowered" one another by utilizing their

00:02:28.130 --> 00:02:31.879
strengths and weaknesses to form a friendship,
rather than turning on one another.

00:02:31.879 --> 00:02:35.469
As she notes, though, parts like that are
harder to come by, and instead what she's

00:02:35.469 --> 00:02:37.629
become known for are roles that play to type.

00:02:37.629 --> 00:02:42.030
In the last decade, Diaz has often played
a variation of the same character: a career

00:02:42.030 --> 00:02:46.940
gal inadvertently marries a party boy in What
Happens in Vegas, a single gal inadvertently

00:02:46.940 --> 00:02:51.180
gets tangled up in a fugitive relationship
with a spy in Knight and Day, and a celebrity

00:02:51.180 --> 00:02:55.060
fitness guru in a Hollywood relationship is
caught off guard by the demands of pregnancy

00:02:55.060 --> 00:02:57.439
in What to Expect When You're Expecting.

00:02:57.439 --> 00:03:02.129
Even as Bad Teacher saw Diaz shift gears into
a feistier mode, it was still just a derivative

00:03:02.129 --> 00:03:04.409
rom-com with a bunch of f-bombs thrown in.

00:03:04.409 --> 00:03:08.010
It's gotten to the point where her career
has become the equivalent of writing a paper

00:03:08.010 --> 00:03:11.920
the night before it's due, knowing you'll
probably get a C on it but accepting that

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:12.959
will be good enough.

00:03:12.959 --> 00:03:16.049
"Things are about to change around here."

00:03:16.049 --> 00:03:19.849
Perhaps Diaz is holding out for something
substantial before she signs on for another

00:03:19.849 --> 00:03:23.859
feature film, or perhaps she's considering
the peak TV scene as a next stop.

00:03:23.859 --> 00:03:27.349
Of course, those close to her seem to think
there's something else going on ...

00:03:27.349 --> 00:03:28.919
Early retirement?

00:03:28.919 --> 00:03:32.549
Actress and longtime friend of Diaz, Selma
Blair, dropped an unintentional bombshell

00:03:32.549 --> 00:03:36.499
about her The Sweetest Thing co-star's career
during a chat with the Evening Standard when

00:03:36.499 --> 00:03:37.499
she said:

00:03:37.499 --> 00:03:40.069
"I had lunch with Cameron the other day, We
were reminiscing about the film.

00:03:40.069 --> 00:03:43.440
I would have liked to do a sequel but Cameron's
retired from acting.

00:03:43.440 --> 00:03:44.499
She's like 'I'm done.'"

00:03:44.499 --> 00:03:48.670
Considering that wasn't exactly public information,
the quote sent the entertainment world into

00:03:48.670 --> 00:03:53.450
an immediate tailspin and made everyone realize
that, yes, Diaz has been absent from the biz

00:03:53.450 --> 00:03:54.450
for a long time.

00:03:54.450 --> 00:03:57.489
Blair did add that she didn't know if it was
a permanent decision, saying:

00:03:57.489 --> 00:03:59.819
"I mean, she doesn't need to make any more
films.

00:03:59.819 --> 00:04:03.239
She has a pretty great life, I don't know
what it would take to bring her back."

00:04:03.239 --> 00:04:07.170
After the resulting commotion, Blair took
to Twitter to clarify her comments, writing:

00:04:07.170 --> 00:04:10.700
"BREAKING NEWS Guys please, I was making a
joke in an interview.

00:04:10.700 --> 00:04:12.480
CAMERON DIAZ is NOT retiring from ANYTHING.

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:17.310
And for more breaking news: I am NOW retiring
from being Cameron Diaz's spokesperson."

00:04:17.310 --> 00:04:18.310
But wait!

00:04:18.310 --> 00:04:22.780
Diaz seemed to confirm her friend's comments
during a March 2018 reunion with The Sweetest

00:04:22.780 --> 00:04:24.030
Things co-stars.

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:28.599
While bantering about family lives with Blair
and Christina Applegate, Diaz said that she's

00:04:28.599 --> 00:04:31.660
"literally doing nothing" and "actually retired."

00:04:31.660 --> 00:04:33.660
Was that an official announcement?

00:04:33.660 --> 00:04:37.030
Considering the comedic chops of all three
of these seasoned actresses, they could very

00:04:37.030 --> 00:04:41.320
well have been toying with our emotions, knowing
the tabloids would flip -- and they did.

00:04:41.320 --> 00:04:43.759
Was Diaz being serious or sarcastic?

00:04:43.759 --> 00:04:47.849
That tiny bit of talk left us craving more
info (and movies) from all three of these

00:04:47.849 --> 00:04:49.000
women.

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:50.000
Settled down

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:55.040
Diaz's previous high-profile relationships
with stars like Matt Dillon, Justin Timberlake,

00:04:55.040 --> 00:04:59.310
and Alex Rodriguez made her a regular feature
of weekly tabloids, but all of that changed

00:04:59.310 --> 00:05:02.630
when she and Good Charlotte guitarist Benji
Madden became an item.

00:05:02.630 --> 00:05:06.780
The two dated for just a few months before
making it official, and Diaz has never sounded

00:05:06.780 --> 00:05:07.780
happier.

00:05:07.780 --> 00:05:10.419
She gushed on Instagram:
"One of my favorite things about being married,

00:05:10.419 --> 00:05:12.280
is how much pride I take in my husband.

00:05:12.280 --> 00:05:13.949
He makes me proud everyday.

00:05:13.949 --> 00:05:17.479
One day it might be how generous and giving,
another how gentle and thoughtful.

00:05:17.479 --> 00:05:20.780
Or when he is fiercely protective of the people
he loves and cares about.

00:05:20.780 --> 00:05:24.560
And every single day I am so incredibly proud
of his integrity as a human being."

00:05:24.560 --> 00:05:28.240
Considering it'd been just a few years since
she said she didn't even believe in monogamy,

00:05:28.240 --> 00:05:33.139
it sounds like this romance took her by surprise
and swept her off her feet and the screen.

00:05:33.139 --> 00:05:34.710
New path

00:05:34.710 --> 00:05:37.759
Diaz's absence from the big screen may have
been deliberate after all.

00:05:37.759 --> 00:05:42.250
Over the last few years, she's been busy carving
out a career for herself as a lifestyle author.

00:05:42.250 --> 00:05:46.400
In 2013, she co-wrote The Body Book, which
quickly became a best-seller.

00:05:46.400 --> 00:05:50.930
On the heels of that success, she released
The Longevity Book in 2016, which addresses

00:05:50.930 --> 00:05:54.990
the science of aging and explores her own
efforts to stay healthy as she gets older.

00:05:54.990 --> 00:05:58.879
"As we get older there are phases of life
that we enter into"

00:05:58.879 --> 00:06:02.250
"What I learned is that aging is really about
living."

00:06:02.250 --> 00:06:05.979
In an interview with Entertainment Weekly,
Diaz revealed something about her motivation

00:06:05.979 --> 00:06:10.479
for writing that could be interpreted as an
increasing disdain with the vanity of Hollywood.

00:06:10.479 --> 00:06:13.949
Asked whether she thought her recommended
"anti-aging techniques" would be viewed through

00:06:13.949 --> 00:06:17.840
the lens of society's diminishing "superficial
value on aging," Diaz replied:

00:06:17.840 --> 00:06:22.099
"I hope people will start to embrace it more
in that way, but I think we do live in a society

00:06:22.099 --> 00:06:26.169
where everywhere you look, every billboard,
every magazine, every advertisement that pops

00:06:26.169 --> 00:06:30.050
up on our computer is telling you where you're
at [in age] is scary and dangerous."

00:06:30.050 --> 00:06:34.479
In other words: Diaz is more focused on personal
wellness these days than she is on conforming

00:06:34.479 --> 00:06:37.480
to a studio's idea of what her body should
look like.

00:06:37.480 --> 00:06:41.870
That's obviously a long overdue revelation
because in 2017, Diaz admitted she'd started

00:06:41.870 --> 00:06:43.220
to lose touch with herself.

00:06:43.220 --> 00:06:46.750
The actress appeared on a panel discussion
at Gwyneth Paltrow's Goop Wellness Summit

00:06:46.750 --> 00:06:51.539
and revealed that being part of the entertainment
business took a toll on her emotional wellbeing,

00:06:51.539 --> 00:06:52.539
saying:

00:06:52.539 --> 00:06:54.460
"I just went, 'I can't really say who I am
to myself.'

00:06:54.460 --> 00:06:55.909
Which is a hard thing to face up to.

00:06:55.909 --> 00:06:57.540
I felt the need to make myself whole."

00:06:57.540 --> 00:07:01.310
This fame fatigue may have prompted studios
to award roles that might have ordinarily

00:07:01.310 --> 00:07:03.479
gone her way to more eager actresses.

00:07:03.479 --> 00:07:07.509
Or it could have been exactly what it sounds
like: an extended mental health sabbatical

00:07:07.509 --> 00:07:11.460
that she certainly earned after two decades
spent maintaining a spot on the A-list.

00:07:11.460 --> 00:07:16.800
In either case, Diaz's current Hollywood hiatus
seems to be mostly on her own terms, so whether

00:07:16.800 --> 00:07:20.509
or not she ever changes her mind, at least
we'll know she's in charge of her own future

00:07:20.509 --> 00:07:21.509
now.

00:07:21.509 --> 00:07:22.509
Thanks for watching!

00:07:22.509 --> 00:07:25.159
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:07:25.159 --> 00:07:27.219
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

